  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b508cb6de8a62cf4aaed2791d93415c0</srcmd5>
    <version>0.5.18</version>
    <time>1787656803</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.5.18.

Upstream removed the torchao integration, so the python-torchao
dependency is dropped. The Rust PyO3 extension modules moved to
sglang.srt.rust_extensions._multimodal and ._grpc; the %check smoke
test follows them. All compiled-kernel caches moved under
SGLANG_CACHE_DIR upstream.

All four patches were rebased. sglang-cpu-triton-stub.patch now
targets _platform_stubs.py, which replaced _triton_stub.py upstream;
it also imports importlib.machinery and importlib.util explicitly,
which Python 3.14 no longer provides implicitly (that part is
upstream sgl-project/sglang PR 36215).

License gains BSD-2-Clause: the numpy crate in the sglang-mm
dependency graph is BSD-2-Clause only.

vendor.tar.zst regenerated. Built and %check-tested locally on
aarch64 for python313 and python314.</comment>
    <requestid>1373479</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>4b2de9f2ab3a75b1a688200b9ba35725</srcmd5>
    <version>0.5.19</version>
    <time>1788879300</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.5.19

Upstream highlights relevant to this CPU build:
- Beam search (beam_width); not combinable with speculative decoding,
  disaggregation, DP attention or HiCache yet
- The unified radix tree becomes the cache for every model;
  SGLANG_ENABLE_UNIFIED_RADIX_TREE is deprecated
- ServerArgs no longer resolves on construction - callers building one
  by hand must call resolve_once()
- Requests capped at 32 stop strings and 32 stop regexes of at most
  256 bytes each, HTTP 400 beyond that
- CPU backend: ERNIE support, NUMA/core binding for DP ranks, plus DP
  attention, bidirectional-attention masking, intel_amx spec verify
  and GPTQ INT4 fused_input_proj fixes

Packaging:
- sglang-cpu-triton-stub.patch rebased (upstream grew the Triton stub
  with autotuner/compiler/GPUTarget classes above our hunk); the other
  three patches apply unchanged
- The #! line is now stripped from every shipped module, not just
  cli/killall.py: 0.5.19 adds srt/model_loader/expert_pack/*.py, which
  carry one but are imported, not executed
- vendor.tar.zst regenerated. Licence re-derived over the shipped
  sglang-mm/sglang-grpc graphs: the only genuinely new crates are
  miniz_oxide (MIT OR Zlib OR Apache-2.0, reachable via flate2) and
  zlib-rs (not in the shipped graph at all), so the License: tag is
  unchanged.

pyproject_cpu.toml is byte-identical to 0.5.18, so no dependency floor
moved - torch stays at the 2.12.0 Factory ships.

Built locally on aarch64 against openSUSE_Tumbleweed: green, %check
imports both Rust PyO3 extensions and runs the CLI for python313 and
python314. rpmlint is at the accepted 0.5.18 baseline (6 errors /
2 warnings / 6 badness, all pre-existing update-alternatives items plus
the outlines Suggests). source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1376136</requestid>
  </revision>
